1
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:34,347
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece

2
00:02:34,347 --> 00:02:37,307
must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

3
00:02:37,307 --> 00:02:41,667
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

4
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:44,747
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,347
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,347 --> 00:02:50,107
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:50,107 --> 00:02:53,027
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:56,627 --> 00:02:58,667
During their journey to the New World,

9
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:01,427
Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island,

10
00:03:01,427 --> 00:03:05,067
which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

11
00:03:05,067 --> 00:03:07,467
The Fishman pirates, led by Horty Jones

12
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:09,427
and assisted by Vander Decken,

13
00:03:09,427 --> 00:03:12,227
plot to overthrow King Neptune.

14
00:03:12,227 --> 00:03:13,867
Friends or enemies, huh?

15
00:03:14,947 --> 00:03:16,107
Don't ask me.

16
00:03:17,107 --> 00:03:20,427
Cause I'd say, it's up to you!

17
00:03:24,307 --> 00:03:25,507
The Big Clash!

18
00:03:25,507 --> 00:03:28,587
The Straw Hats versus 100,000 Enemies!

19
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:29,907
The Big Clash!

20
00:03:34,907 --> 00:03:37,067
Uh, hey guys, is that him?

21
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:38,227
I really hope not,

22
00:03:38,227 --> 00:03:40,707
cause he's invaded the Navy headquarters twice,

23
00:03:40,707 --> 00:03:41,907
and we're no Navy!

24
00:03:42,547 --> 00:03:44,747
Well, that looks like his pirate ship.

25
00:03:44,747 --> 00:03:47,027
Not to mention his crew, so yeah.

26
00:03:58,667 --> 00:03:59,027
the années in Physics.

27
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:05,627
Ha ha ha!

28
00:04:14,507 --> 00:04:15,647
Ha, come on really?

29
00:04:15,647 --> 00:04:17,687
What kind of weirdo hides inside a shark?

30
00:04:18,127 --> 00:04:22,887
I'm more concerned with how that skeleton and the others managed to escape from the Ryugu Palace.

31
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:25,547
About time you showed up, Straw Hat!

32
00:04:25,687 --> 00:04:26,887
I can't believe he came!

33
00:04:27,487 --> 00:04:30,307
Madam Shirley! That pirate you were talking about!

34
00:04:30,547 --> 00:04:31,427
He's here!

35
00:04:31,687 --> 00:04:33,967
Yeah, he just saved the princess and the king!

36
00:04:34,787 --> 00:04:36,307
The Straw Hat Boy.

37
00:04:41,047 --> 00:04:43,547
Yeah, yeah, I'm here. How was that?

38
00:04:43,547 --> 00:04:46,387
It could have gone worse, considering it was Luffy.

39
00:04:46,847 --> 00:04:50,947
Hmm. Not exactly what we had planned, but I can't argue with the results.

40
00:04:54,047 --> 00:04:56,647
No! You're staying right here!

41
00:04:56,807 --> 00:04:59,287
Don't fight. It's pointless.

42
00:04:59,787 --> 00:05:01,967
Come on. We're just wasting time.

43
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:05,607
Yes, right. If we don't hurry, they'll kill father.

44
00:05:05,827 --> 00:05:10,687
I already told you, Jinbei! Get out of my way so I can go and kick this horny guy's ass!

45
00:05:10,687 --> 00:05:13,887
And I told you to wait! You aren't listening at all!

46
00:05:14,287 --> 00:05:15,407
Let me finish speaking!

47
00:05:16,207 --> 00:05:18,927
Now, how would you describe the relationship between us?

48
00:05:19,187 --> 00:05:19,887
We're friends.

49
00:05:20,347 --> 00:05:21,067
That's right.

50
00:05:21,067 --> 00:05:28,067
Although it is a simple matter for us, our two peoples have been struggling to establish such a relationship for decades now.

51
00:05:28,567 --> 00:05:34,027
I left you a message saying not to fight Horty, because I didn't want you facing him recklessly.

52
00:05:34,707 --> 00:05:35,527
Don't you see?

53
00:05:35,527 --> 00:05:38,387
Horty, think of how the fishmen will view you.

54
00:05:38,747 --> 00:05:45,067
If you rush in and show aggression towards Horty, you'll be viewed as nothing more than just another human bully oppressing our kind.

55
00:05:45,647 --> 00:05:46,927
That is not what we want.

56
00:05:47,387 --> 00:05:48,927
No! You should be a hero!

57
00:05:49,487 --> 00:05:51,087
One that saves the island!

58
00:05:51,087 --> 00:05:55,747
A hero? Hell no!

59
00:05:55,987 --> 00:05:56,667
Why why?

60
00:05:57,007 --> 00:05:58,767
Obviously because we're pirates!

61
00:05:58,987 --> 00:06:00,747
Come on! Heroes are great!

62
00:06:01,307 --> 00:06:02,427
But I'm not one!

63
00:06:04,087 --> 00:06:04,567
Seriously!

64
00:06:04,987 --> 00:06:07,027
Do you even know what you're asking me to do?

65
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,807
Let's say there's a chunk of meat, right?

66
00:06:10,547 --> 00:06:12,887
Pirates will have a banquet and dig right in.

67
00:06:13,107 --> 00:06:16,067
But a hero would give it to other people instead of eating it!

68
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:18,407
Screw that! My meat is mine!

69
00:06:18,407 --> 00:06:20,947
What a reason.

70
00:06:22,427 --> 00:06:24,107
It figures, dummy.

71
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:28,047
Luffy! I'll let you have all the meat you want! Just do as I say!

72
00:06:28,907 --> 00:06:29,567
That's fair.

73
00:06:30,627 --> 00:06:31,407
No way!

74
00:06:32,107 --> 00:06:33,107
I'll make this simple.

75
00:06:33,667 --> 00:06:37,847
There will come a time when I need your help so you'll rush in when that moment arrives.

76
00:06:38,287 --> 00:06:38,807
Okay.

77
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:39,487
Good.

78
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:41,807
But first, the plan.

79
00:06:42,067 --> 00:06:45,047
We'll get caught, on purpose, to get us close.

80
00:06:45,047 --> 00:06:55,767
Afterwards, while their attention's on me, then one of you pirates will sneak out of Megalo's stomach and get yourself into position to make your attack.

81
00:06:56,107 --> 00:06:57,347
Did you say a stomach?

82
00:06:57,347 --> 00:07:06,327
The Celestial Dragon's letter. They have it. We need it.

83
00:07:06,947 --> 00:07:08,967
Hold on. What's this letter?

84
00:07:09,507 --> 00:07:14,887
Jinbei, remember? Luffy was sleeping through most of your story. He doesn't know.

85
00:07:14,887 --> 00:07:24,567
In short, the letter is something Queen Otohime acquired ten years ago at great personal risk. It will define the very future of this island.

86
00:07:25,427 --> 00:07:28,607
They'll also have the key we'll need to release the king from his bonds.

87
00:07:29,287 --> 00:07:31,207
One of your crewmates must retrieve them.

88
00:07:31,847 --> 00:07:33,687
Which one of you's up to the task?

89
00:07:33,687 --> 00:07:37,767
I'm pretty good at stealing, but still, I think I'll need Robin's help.

90
00:07:38,507 --> 00:07:39,127
Of course.

91
00:07:40,247 --> 00:07:45,247
Good. Once you've managed to free the king, get out. I'll call Luffy and we'll take over.

92
00:07:45,907 --> 00:07:50,507
After you emerge from Megalo's body, the people of Fishman Island will understand your intent.

93
00:07:51,167 --> 00:07:54,467
Because they'll see you and I working together against the common foe.

94
00:07:54,467 --> 00:08:00,487
Princess, I must ask that you stay somewhere safe outside the plaza. It's for the best.

95
00:08:00,907 --> 00:08:05,147
We'll pass the letter to you, whereupon the entire royal family can't escape.

96
00:08:05,907 --> 00:08:11,387
During this time, the rest of you will have to head to Ryugu Palace to rescue your imprisoned friends.

97
00:08:12,387 --> 00:08:16,487
Once they're free, get to the plaza to back us up as soon as possible.

98
00:08:17,307 --> 00:08:23,107
As for how you go about saving them, well, that's for you to deal with.

99
00:08:23,107 --> 00:08:24,687
Come on! Be specific!

100
00:08:25,627 --> 00:08:28,267
Wow! You can count on us big time!

101
00:08:28,427 --> 00:08:30,607
After all, we've got the Sunny, right?

102
00:08:31,227 --> 00:08:33,387
So no worries. We'll be there.

103
00:08:34,827 --> 00:08:39,787
Once this is set in motion, there's no turning back. We must succeed!

104
00:08:40,267 --> 00:08:43,447
You, everyone here, respects Jinbei.

105
00:08:43,927 --> 00:08:47,767
Whether they're a civilian or outlaw, they'll follow after his example.

106
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:55,827
Mm-hmm. That's right. So if they see Jinbei working with a human, even a pirate, they'll cheer you on or maybe even fight beside you.

107
00:08:56,347 --> 00:08:57,547
I mean, it's possible.

108
00:08:59,227 --> 00:09:00,067
Straw hat?

109
00:09:01,327 --> 00:09:02,187
Please, Luffy.

110
00:09:02,187 --> 00:09:12,727
I'm only doing this because you asked me to. Got that? I mean it! Having people cheer for me? No thanks! I don't like it!

111
00:09:12,867 --> 00:09:15,287
I'm more for taking their money and running away.

112
00:09:15,747 --> 00:09:20,627
Speak for yourselves! I'd go to the depths of hell if I knew the mermaids would be there to cheer me on!

113
00:09:21,067 --> 00:09:22,167
Very well, then.

114
00:09:23,047 --> 00:09:24,787
Sounds like everything is settled, then.

115
00:09:25,507 --> 00:09:27,507
All right. Let's do this thing!

116
00:09:27,507 --> 00:09:29,487
Hmm. Wait.

117
00:09:30,387 --> 00:09:32,467
Yeah? What's up? Something wrong?

118
00:09:33,367 --> 00:09:34,627
What's our codename?

119
00:09:34,807 --> 00:09:36,487
Are you kidding? Who cares?

120
00:09:36,987 --> 00:09:38,227
Can we go already?

121
00:09:40,287 --> 00:09:44,667
At any rate, it appears you were able to save your friends from the palace.

122
00:09:45,267 --> 00:09:45,967
Straw hat!

123
00:09:46,787 --> 00:09:48,107
Huh? Papa Goo!

124
00:09:48,747 --> 00:09:50,727
What's up? It hasn't been that long.

125
00:09:50,927 --> 00:09:55,027
I know, I know! But I almost died! Many times! Because of those guys!

126
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:55,467
Huh?

127
00:09:55,467 --> 00:10:00,587
That's straw hat Luffy! He's human! And a pirate! But on our side!

128
00:10:01,007 --> 00:10:04,027
He showed up right when Princess Shirohoshi called for him!

129
00:10:04,287 --> 00:10:08,547
From the looks of things, he's here to help us Jinbei save the country from Hordi's men!

130
00:10:08,967 --> 00:10:09,887
Shirohat!

131
00:10:12,247 --> 00:10:14,307
Isn't it sweet how they cling to you?

132
00:10:14,707 --> 00:10:17,107
But you've only delayed the king's inevitable demise!

133
00:10:18,107 --> 00:10:20,687
After all, you are nothing but a human!

134
00:10:21,647 --> 00:10:24,387
Your beauty outshines all others, princess!

135
00:10:24,387 --> 00:10:30,407
Now that we've met, would you be willing to show me your panties?

136
00:10:30,407 --> 00:10:33,207
You can't ask her that!

137
00:10:33,527 --> 00:10:34,887
Then show me yours!

138
00:10:35,107 --> 00:10:36,407
No way in hell!

139
00:10:39,947 --> 00:10:42,287
Okay, we're back! About time!

140
00:10:42,507 --> 00:10:43,927
They're all ignoring you!

141
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:47,267
That's just because I was using my inside voice!

142
00:10:47,687 --> 00:10:48,527
Nami Swan!

143
00:10:49,207 --> 00:10:52,827
Now that I've saved those idiots from the palace, you have to love me!

144
00:10:52,827 --> 00:10:53,827
Right?

145
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:54,407
Whatever!

146
00:10:55,287 --> 00:10:59,287
Wait, he did what? Liar? We got to the exit ourselves!

147
00:11:00,547 --> 00:11:04,347
Maybe! However, you never would have escaped! Without me!

148
00:11:04,487 --> 00:11:06,167
That's a joke! Right, you guys?

149
00:11:06,247 --> 00:11:07,467
Wish I could say it was!

150
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,747
But he left out the part where Brooke was a ghost!

151
00:11:10,207 --> 00:11:11,127
What'd you say?

152
00:11:11,247 --> 00:11:12,267
You heard right!

153
00:11:12,527 --> 00:11:15,807
Our escape was only possible because of my splendid new ability!

154
00:11:15,807 --> 00:11:24,587
I need you to find the key! I mean, I need you to find the sword!

155
00:11:25,367 --> 00:11:25,867
Please!

156
00:11:25,867 --> 00:11:26,787
There's no time!

157
00:11:26,887 --> 00:11:27,947
Stay away, ghost!

158
00:11:31,987 --> 00:11:32,867
I'm a ghost!

159
00:11:35,707 --> 00:11:43,467
All right, that's weird. How exactly does this ghost know my name?

160
00:11:43,467 --> 00:11:45,987
Come now! We're friends!

161
00:11:46,147 --> 00:11:46,867
Yo-ho-ho-ho!

162
00:11:47,007 --> 00:11:50,307
Ah! No, we're not! I don't have any friends that are ghosts!

163
00:11:51,067 --> 00:11:53,907
Wait, you're Boondaddy, aren't you?

164
00:11:54,327 --> 00:11:56,587
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

165
00:12:05,807 --> 00:12:07,767
Oh no! It's here!

166
00:12:08,667 --> 00:12:10,467
What are you doing, Brooke? Hurry!

167
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:12,927
Before it's too late!

168
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:15,467
I feel sorry for the wait!

169
00:12:15,467 --> 00:12:17,467
Oh, no biggie!

170
00:12:17,467 --> 00:12:18,467
Ow!

171
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:20,467
Here! Your sword!

172
00:12:32,467 --> 00:12:34,467
Nice cut! Way to go!

173
00:12:34,467 --> 00:12:36,467
Heck yeah! We're outta here!

174
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:38,467
Three-sword style!

175
00:12:38,467 --> 00:12:40,467
Okay, that was way too much!

176
00:12:40,467 --> 00:12:41,467
You think?

177
00:12:41,467 --> 00:12:43,467
I'm running out of strength!

178
00:12:43,467 --> 00:12:44,467
I gotta get a breath!

179
00:12:44,467 --> 00:12:45,467
Damn!

180
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:46,467
I'm gonna die!

181
00:12:46,467 --> 00:12:47,467
I'm gonna die!

182
00:12:47,467 --> 00:12:48,467
Ow!

183
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:49,467
What the heck?

184
00:12:49,467 --> 00:12:50,467
Hey! I came to get ya!

185
00:12:50,467 --> 00:12:51,467
Great, they're still alive!

186
00:12:51,467 --> 00:12:52,467
It was very exciting!

187
00:12:52,467 --> 00:12:53,467
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

188
00:12:53,467 --> 00:12:54,467
It sounds like your new ability is still alive!

189
00:12:54,467 --> 00:12:55,467
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

190
00:12:55,467 --> 00:12:56,467
It sounds like your new ability is still alive!

191
00:12:56,467 --> 00:12:57,467
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

192
00:12:57,467 --> 00:12:58,467
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

193
00:12:58,467 --> 00:13:01,467
I'm running out of strength!

194
00:13:01,467 --> 00:13:02,467
Oh, I'm running out of strength!

195
00:13:02,467 --> 00:13:03,467
I-I gotta get a breath!

196
00:13:03,467 --> 00:13:04,467
Damn!

197
00:13:04,467 --> 00:13:06,467
I'm gonna die!

198
00:13:06,467 --> 00:13:07,467
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

199
00:13:07,467 --> 00:13:09,467
What the heck?!

200
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,467
Hey! I came to get ya!

201
00:13:11,467 --> 00:13:12,467
Great, they're still alive!

202
00:13:12,467 --> 00:13:13,467
It was very exciting!

203
00:13:13,467 --> 00:13:16,467
It sounds like your new ability is pretty amazing, Brooke!

204
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:19,467
I'm sure it'll come in handy!

205
00:13:19,467 --> 00:13:21,467
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

206
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:23,467
It sounds like your new ability is pretty amazing, Brooke!

207
00:13:23,467 --> 00:13:25,467
I'm sure it'll come in handy!

208
00:13:25,467 --> 00:13:32,787
come in handy. Anyway, Luffy knocked their captain out in one hit. Why don't they seem

209
00:13:32,787 --> 00:13:36,927
more worried about that? You're right. That's odd.

210
00:13:55,467 --> 00:14:01,627
Shira Hoshi, it's your mom's letter. Here you go.

211
00:14:02,627 --> 00:14:07,567
I can't tell you how much this means to me. I know it may look like an ordinary piece

212
00:14:07,567 --> 00:14:10,067
of paper, but it's this island's hope.

213
00:14:10,407 --> 00:14:13,347
That's enough. Weepy Hoshi, it's not safe.

214
00:14:14,547 --> 00:14:20,007
He's right. You weren't meant to be caught, so you must leave. Now, while you can.

215
00:14:21,107 --> 00:14:24,007
Wait, Luffy. What, did you call me?

216
00:14:24,007 --> 00:14:29,107
Huh? Just now, it was almost my name, but...

217
00:14:29,107 --> 00:14:33,907
Yeah, I was wrong about you. You're a wuss, but more than just a crybaby.

218
00:14:34,327 --> 00:14:38,127
So I'll call you Weepy Hoshi. It's an upgrade.

219
00:14:39,167 --> 00:14:43,847
When a person feels as if they've been wronged, well, then it's only natural that they would

220
00:14:43,847 --> 00:14:46,047
turn to hate. That man.

221
00:14:47,967 --> 00:14:50,307
Hordy. He's doing exactly that.

222
00:14:50,307 --> 00:14:58,767
But you chose not to hate. A coward wouldn't do that. Hardship has only made you stronger

223
00:14:58,767 --> 00:14:59,387
in the end.

224
00:14:59,867 --> 00:15:05,407
Nami is right. You endured. Princess, I'm proud of you.

225
00:15:05,407 --> 00:15:10,607
I appreciate the thought. But still, I feel like I caused everyone trouble by keeping

226
00:15:10,607 --> 00:15:11,827
this secret to myself.

227
00:15:12,227 --> 00:15:15,467
I'm sorry. You're mistaken. You've done quite well.

228
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:21,267
Your intentions were pure. Just like those who have come before you.

229
00:15:21,267 --> 00:15:25,507
You can't tell them you have to hold it in.

230
00:15:26,447 --> 00:15:32,087
Listen. Don't become angry on my behalf. I don't want that.

231
00:15:34,087 --> 00:15:39,567
Our heroes planted a seed in your heart, and it has blossomed beautifully. You have lived

232
00:15:39,567 --> 00:15:45,767
by their example well. If everyone else thought the way you do, then there would be no more

233
00:15:45,767 --> 00:15:51,847
fighting, and the conflict between fishmen and humans would be over at last. You may have

234
00:15:51,847 --> 00:15:55,427
suffered through those past years alone, but that doesn't make that time meaningless.

235
00:15:56,767 --> 00:16:02,587
Single-handedly, you are a defender, protecting the virtues of others day after day.

236
00:16:03,767 --> 00:16:07,567
But today, we're here. We'll protect them for you.

237
00:16:07,567 --> 00:16:29,567
Thank you.

238
00:16:29,567 --> 00:16:35,567
Thank you so much.

239
00:16:35,567 --> 00:16:42,027
You're still a crybaby. That's for sure.

240
00:16:43,027 --> 00:16:45,287
Strahat! Take him down!

241
00:16:48,767 --> 00:16:54,187
I should have known Vander Decken was going to fail me. He couldn't even get rid of one

242
00:16:54,187 --> 00:16:55,307
lousy princess.

243
00:16:56,307 --> 00:16:57,547
Captain Horty!

244
00:16:57,547 --> 00:17:02,067
It's as I thought. The energy steroid is still coursing through his veins.

245
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:05,527
Given how much he took, I'd be surprised if it wasn't!

246
00:17:05,527 --> 00:17:08,527
He's back up! They're done for!

247
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:28,367
Her power is too great. It really is the stuff of legends. Once I found out it was real, I knew I had to eliminate her as soon as possible.

248
00:17:28,367 --> 00:17:40,367
Sir. But then, you got in my way. Admittedly, I should have known something was wrong when you were captured without putting up a fight, Jinbei.

249
00:17:40,367 --> 00:17:48,827
You really like these humans, don't you? People like you were the worst. You've completely forgotten your pride.

250
00:17:48,827 --> 00:17:57,827
See? You grew up with Tiger in our district. And let's not forget Arlong. He was like your brother. Both of them were beaten or killed by humans.

251
00:17:57,827 --> 00:18:09,827
But instead of avenging them, you wouldn't get in bed with the humans. It's pathetic. Jinbei, godless like Neptune. But soon, everything is going to change.

252
00:18:09,827 --> 00:18:16,827
Once I'm king, that is. Hear that? I'll start with the world summit. That'll be the perfect place.

253
00:18:16,827 --> 00:18:29,827
With every ruler in the surface world in one place, they'll be easy to kill. Then the whole world will learn to fear our underwater kingdom.

254
00:18:29,827 --> 00:18:40,827
Their kingdoms in disarray will drag the humans into the depths and enslave every last one. In time, there won't be a soul left to stand against us. And we will rule the great pirate era.

255
00:18:40,827 --> 00:18:54,827
Oh, yes. You pirates. Wheel-pow. The same as everybody else. Just you wait. You see? These humans are more than capable of holding their own, yet they kneel before me.

256
00:18:55,827 --> 00:19:04,827
That's right. In a moment, you'll be just like them. Straw hats. I'll be king of the fishmen, king of the humans, and king of the pirates.

257
00:19:04,827 --> 00:19:07,827
Is that so?

258
00:19:07,827 --> 00:19:19,827
And to think there are only ten of you here to stand in my way. What can you possibly do when we're 100,000?

259
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:29,827
How are they supposed to fight all of them? Boss Jinbei's side is too outnumbered. I don't like these odds. Are they going to be okay?

260
00:19:29,827 --> 00:19:38,827
They're the only hope we have left. So if they lose, Horty takes everything. They must win. Because if they don't, that march is going to take our homes away.

261
00:19:38,827 --> 00:19:41,827
Fight! Boss Jinbei! You got this, Straw Hat!

262
00:19:41,827 --> 00:19:42,827
Straw Hat!

263
00:19:43,827 --> 00:19:45,827
Kill them! New fishmen pirates!

264
00:19:48,827 --> 00:19:53,827
Here they come! No way we can fight this many at once! We're done for!

265
00:19:53,827 --> 00:19:57,827
This is exactly the reason I don't like hanging out with you guys!

266
00:19:58,827 --> 00:20:01,827
Before this begins, it's been a pleasure traveling with all of you.

267
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:03,827
Don't say that! Gah!

268
00:20:04,827 --> 00:20:12,827
There are so many enemies. Wow. If I try to count them all, my eyes may pop out. Then again, I don't have eyes. So they can't!

269
00:20:12,827 --> 00:20:17,827
Just 100,000? That's nothing we can't handle, right?

270
00:20:18,827 --> 00:20:22,827
Hey, wait! You're just saying that because you're hiding behind us!

271
00:20:23,827 --> 00:20:29,827
And here I go! It's time to shine! Super armored me! All right!

272
00:20:30,827 --> 00:20:32,827
Let's do this already! Get over here!

273
00:20:33,827 --> 00:20:38,827
In case you can't count, we're each going to have to take down 10,000 of these guys to win this fight.

274
00:20:38,827 --> 00:20:46,827
They have numbers, but it doesn't make them stronger. I mean, it's not like they're Navy Admirals or anything. So don't crap yourself.

275
00:20:47,827 --> 00:20:53,827
After these guys, you're next! Number 10,001! Bring it on! I can't wait!

276
00:20:57,827 --> 00:20:58,827
Hey, Luffy!

277
00:20:59,827 --> 00:21:00,827
Oh, no!

278
00:21:01,827 --> 00:21:02,827
Luffy?

279
00:21:03,827 --> 00:21:05,827
Those 4 million berries are mine!

280
00:21:06,827 --> 00:21:08,827
No, they're mine! It's too easy!

281
00:21:11,827 --> 00:21:12,827
Kill him!

282
00:21:32,827 --> 00:21:33,827
Son of a bash!

283
00:21:46,827 --> 00:21:47,267
skill 3

284
00:21:47,827 --> 00:21:48,227
ah! What the hell just happened!

285
00:21:48,827 --> 00:21:51,827
Ah! What the hell just happened!

286
00:21:54,827 --> 00:21:56,827
And now we're in person, he's got an eye to nose!

287
00:21:56,827 --> 00:22:10,767
But he didn't do anything, and he still knocked them all out!

288
00:22:11,027 --> 00:22:13,567
Hey! Get up, guys! Come on!

289
00:22:13,627 --> 00:22:16,387
Damn! He took down half of us in an instant!

290
00:22:16,787 --> 00:22:20,067
That was 50,000 of our men! What did he even do?

291
00:22:20,847 --> 00:22:22,447
Did everyone see that?

292
00:22:22,667 --> 00:22:25,367
Yeah, but I don't know what it was!

293
00:22:25,367 --> 00:22:26,467
So much power.

294
00:22:26,827 --> 00:22:27,847
For one so young.

295
00:22:28,147 --> 00:22:30,907
Wait! Did the Straw Hat guy really do that?

296
00:22:31,487 --> 00:22:32,767
Yeah! Too cool!

297
00:22:33,387 --> 00:22:34,927
That hockey...

298
00:22:34,927 --> 00:22:37,047
That training paid off, I see.

299
00:22:37,707 --> 00:22:41,447
Unreal. I mean, Conqueror's hockey? Scary.

300
00:22:41,627 --> 00:22:45,667
Sure is, but I'd expect no less. Otherwise, he couldn't be my captain.

301
00:22:46,187 --> 00:22:48,407
Oh my! Wilfite!

302
00:22:48,627 --> 00:22:52,287
Your name's Hordy, right? I'm about to kick your ass.

303
00:22:52,847 --> 00:22:55,507
You want to become the king of a country or whatever?

304
00:22:55,507 --> 00:22:56,847
Fine, I don't care.

305
00:22:58,787 --> 00:23:00,367
But king of the pirates?

306
00:23:00,867 --> 00:23:02,947
Nuh-uh. That's my job.

307
00:23:02,947 --> 00:23:12,547
Despite Luffy's display of hockey, the sheer number of Hordy's forces proves overwhelming.

308
00:23:12,947 --> 00:23:18,047
As the new Fishman pirates close in on Shirahoshi, Zoro and Sanji launch an assault.

309
00:23:18,427 --> 00:23:23,047
With the last two years still fresh in their minds, the Straw Hat's training is put to the test,

310
00:23:23,047 --> 00:23:26,147
as they unleash a flurry of fearsome new techniques.

311
00:23:26,607 --> 00:23:28,027
On the next, One Piece!

312
00:23:28,427 --> 00:23:30,267
Deadly attacks one after another!

313
00:23:30,727 --> 00:23:32,627
Zoro and Sanji join the battle!

314
00:23:33,007 --> 00:23:34,607
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

315
00:23:34,607 --> 00:23:47,747
Deadly attacks two after another!

